# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Production build values — COMMITTED ON PURPOSE.
#
# Next loads this file for `next build` / `next start` (NODE_ENV=production).
# `.env.local` takes precedence over it, so a developer or a preview deployment
# can still override any value here without editing this file.
#
# NOTHING SECRET MAY EVER BE ADDED HERE. This file is in version control and
# every NEXT_PUBLIC_* value is inlined into the browser bundle anyway. The API
# origin, the Google client ID and anything credential-shaped stay out of it and
# are set per environment.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The canonical public origin of the storefront. Makes `metadataBase` resolve
# canonical and Open Graph URLs to absolute addresses — a relative canonical is
# accepted by crawlers but an absolute one is unambiguous, and og:url must be
# absolute to be useful when a link is shared.
#
# This is a public fact about the site, not configuration that varies by secret,
# which is why it is committed rather than left for someone to remember.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://panchvastra.com
